<title>DENMARK: Danish February trade surplus 3.081 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish February trade surplus 3.081 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 3.081 billion crowns in February 1997, the national statistics office said on Monday.  </p>
<p>It compared to a revised 1.243 billion crowns surplus in January. Seasonally adjusted the surplus was 3.180 billion crowns in February, compared to January's 2.649 billion crowns. DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     Feb 1997	Jan 1997    Feb 1996</p>
<p>Exports			25.715	  26.221	22.932</p>
<p>Imports			22.472	  24.534	20.868</p>
<p>Trade balance excl ships  3.081	   1.243	1.611</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>balance excluding ships   3.180	   2.649	1.906</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average seasonally-adjusted Feb trade surplus excl. ships of 2.1 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
